@startuml
title VEL | Configuration-Driven Source Addition
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #4F5D75
skinparam activityBorderColor #2D3142
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityFontColor #2D3142
skinparam diamondBorderColor #4F5D75
skinparam diamondBackgroundColor #ECECEC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #BFC0C0

start
:Define Input Interface Definition
(RawEvidenceSchema) for the module's state;
:Define Normalization Mapping
(EvidenceNormalizationRule) for the module's state;
#FFF1E9:Implement a thin <Module>FieldBindings adapter
(implements shared IStateFieldBindingProvider)
that reads the module's state via its S-CORE API;
stop

note right
No new Mapper, Validator, or Normalizer class is written.
ConfigDrivenStateMapper, SchemaValidator, and
NormalizationProcessor are shared, config-driven
infrastructure (see Collector_common_class_diagram.puml).
No changes to common VEL processing behavior
are required (FR-VEL-012, FR-VEL-013/014/015).
end note
@enduml
